WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Good morning John, and good morning Alice, and welcome to Earth.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:09.300
It's a wonderful, terrible place and you are a member of its most wonderful and terrible species.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.300
and you're being born into what may  be the most interesting time in human history.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.220
If all goes well within your lifetime, humans will walk on Mars, computers will become intelligent

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.780
The paralyzed will walk again, absolute poverty will be all but eliminated, and you, Alice, may very well live

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.660
to be over 100 years of age!

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.960
Or maybe this advanced, peculiar, unique institution of human technological society

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.780
will implode, taking all humans and a good piece of the Earth with it.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.080
It could go either way really.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.580
In any case, both you and I will be a part of that future.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.780
But luckily you don't really have to worry about any of that right now.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.320
Because you are a baby.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.320
You just have to just have to worry about being a baby.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.320
But nobody ever said that being a baby is easy,

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.680
And so I, your Uncle Hank, have created a simply guide to how to be a baby in six easy steps.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.560
One: You are stuck out here so get used to it.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.940
You probably don't know this because you are a human baby,

00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:00.260
but human babies are born pretty premature when compared to other placental mammals.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.320
This is because our heads have evolved to be super big and their hard to get out of the mom,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.740
after a certain point of development.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.320
So your basically still an embryo, which is really unpleasant.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.500
To be outside of the mother at that point,

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.580
so it's gotta suck.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.140
You're gonna wanna be swaddled and warm.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.140
And you're gonna want wushing noises and stuff like that.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.480
So I suggest, that you just cry until that stuff happens.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:20.920
Speaking of crying,

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:24.700
you will discover that making a really terrible noise is actually very easy for you.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.400
It's basically just like making any other noise.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.340
But you're gonna want to look like it's really difficult.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.920
Like, squint your face up. Get it all red and puffy and cry.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.960
Your vocal cords, right now, are designed to tap directly into your parents sympathy centers

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.260
So that's going to be a useful tool for you.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.780
Three: I would suggest you do a lot of sleeping,

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.380
but not in, like, normal human ways.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.060
You're gonna wanna sleep for about two and a half hours at a time.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.760
That way your parents will approach, but never quite achieve REM sleep.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.580
Which is going to be hilarious when they start having hallucinations.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.440
Four: Put stuff in your mouth.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:59.900
Turns out, because we are so underdeveloped as newborn babies,

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.440
your nervous system is really terrible.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.740
So our complicated sensing is really only right around here.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.580
So if you want to know what something is you just go *arphm*

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.500
(muffled)This is really all you need to know.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.000
Five: Communication is the key to any effective relationship.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.140
You really only have two ways to communicate right now.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.760
One is the crying which we've discussed previously.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.200
Crying is something you're gonna wanna do, just, whenever.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.460
Pretty much all the time.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:24.040
Doesn't matter really how you're feeling.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.300
Hungry. Sleepy. Thirsty. You don't like that smell.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.800
Your butt feels weird.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:29.920
You're just bored.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:30.420
Cry.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.400
Just cry in all of those situations.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.240
But number six, you have another communicative tool.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.100
One you want to be more sparring with,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.080
because it is extremely powerful.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.160
And that,

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.620
is your cuteness.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.940
Be careful with your cute.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.140
It is EXTREMELY potent.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:49.440
Your cute is not just about inspiring love and devotion and getting pinches on the cheeks,

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.740
and saying people saying "I, so, baby, da da!"

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.460
Your cute is the key to our hope.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.940
Our ability to see beyond our own life span.

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:03.400
To feel as if we are part of a continuum that stretches back to the first self replicating life forms.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.160
Your cute reminds us that the decisions we make now,

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.920
will someday effect you and your children and your children's children.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.800
And that you are the next step, and hopefully a better step, in this wonderful, terrible process

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.480
that we call humanity.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.020
I hope that's not too much pressure.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.860
Alice, I wish that I could see you right now.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.840
And hold you go *rasberry* all over your belly.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.260
John, I also wish that I could see you but I won't for a little while.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.240
But, Craig I will see you on Tuesday.

